Dia dhuit, mo chara; a cough that sits heavy on the chest is no joke when the air turns damp like this. I've a bundle of dried thyme and horehound hanging by the hearth that I'll boil up into a strong tea with a spoon of honey to ease her breathing. Bring her round to my fire later so I can listen to her chest proper, for we must be sure it hasn't settled deeper.
